*.jl.cov
*.jl.*.cov
*.jl.mem
*~
.DS_Store
.vscode/

# Documenter.jl build output/lockfile (docs/ -- API reference)
/docs/build/
/docs/Manifest.toml

# Quarto site build output/cache (manual/ -- description, architecture, tutorial)
#
# `manual/docs/` is deliberately NOT ignored, unlike every other build product here. The
# paragraph-search tutorial executes Julia against corpora that are themselves gitignored --
# 827k paragraphs, an hour and a network connection to rebuild -- so no CI can render it. The
# rendered HTML is the only form of that page that can be published, which makes it source for
# publishing purposes even though it is output for every other purpose. Re-render and commit it
# when the pages change, one page at a time:
#
#     XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=$(mktemp -d) quarto render manual/index.qmd
#
# Never `quarto render manual` (the whole project): it empties manual/docs/ first and then dies
# on paragraph-search.qmd's julia engine, leaving the committed site half deleted.
/manual/.quarto/
/manual/_freeze/
**/*.quarto_ipynb

# Manifests are not committed for a package: this repository's own resolve pins the base
# libraries to relative dev checkouts (`path = "../SimilaritySearch.jl"`), which exist on the
# author's machine and nowhere else -- a CI runner or anybody cloning the repository cannot
# instantiate them. Dependencies are declared in Project.toml's [compat] and resolved from the
# General registry, where the whole chain (SimilaritySearch, TextSearch, RocksDB, RocksDB_jll,
# Avro) is published. Keep your local Manifest.toml as the dev-checkout environment it is.
/Manifest.toml
/test/Manifest.toml

# The server subpackage's runtime state -- RocksDB databases, job and cursor spools -- which is
# never source and always local. Anchored so it cannot also match test/data/ or server/test/data/,
# which are fixtures.
/server/data/
/server/workdir/
/server/Manifest.toml
/server/docs/build/

# The Python client's virtualenv and build droppings
server/python/venv/
server/python/**/__pycache__/
server/python/**/*.egg-info/
*.pyc
